From: Upstream kmscon (kmscon/kmscon#540, fixes #539)
Subject: [PATCH] uterm: vt_libseat: adapt log_libseat() to the new log_submit()

Commit efda2b5 (PR #523, "log: Simplify logging") removed LOG_DEFAULT and changed
log_submit() to (severity, subsystem, format, args), but did not update vt_libseat.c,
so the file does not compile with -Dlibseat=enabled (issue #539). This is the upstream
fix (PR #540), taken for the 10.0.4 release which does not have it. Drop it once the
package moves to a release that does.

---
 src/uterm/vt_libseat.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/uterm/vt_libseat.c
+++ b/src/uterm/vt_libseat.c
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@
 
 static void log_libseat(enum libseat_log_level level, const char *fmt, va_list args)
 {
-	log_submit(LOG_DEFAULT, log_level(level), fmt, args);
+	log_submit(log_level(level), "libseat", fmt, args);
 }
 
 static void vt_libseat_input(struct input *input, struct input_key_event *ev, void *data)
